# Ruling OD-2: a SCHEDULED job holds the one-active-job slot, enforced by the database. The fault drops 'scheduled' from the partial unique index predicate (the Phase 1 rule); a second scheduled job is then ALLOWED and the test must say so.
GATE=slot-scheduled
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestConstraints_Jobs (database integration test, real Postgres)
CMD=H_PG_ADMIN_DSN="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" bash tests/harness/run-db-tests.sh '^TestConstraints_Jobs$'
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestConstraints_Jobs
MESSAGE=a second scheduled m1 job for the same user while a scheduled one holds the slot: was ALLOWED
